E = {
    14: "The devil drags one of his hooves through the ground, dragging it with a deadly weight of intention. The devil shoots across the ground, charging at Samson. Samson looks up with his heavy head in exhaustion, unprepared. The concussive blow rings loudly and pushes through his head. The weight of his head is slung across his neck. His head bounces off the dirt once before skedaddling into one smaller jump and a stop. A tooth is now loose in his mouth, reminding him of a familiar haunted flash from the clouds before his death.",
    20: "The weight and crushing feel as if a hole will be pushed through the center of his chest, almost through him and onto the dirt below. Samson, now with enough blood out of the way, starts trumpeting a roaring battle cry, remembering the soul he fights for, and it strips away at his vocals with a scratching and shredding.",
    28: "The spear grows longer as it lies in the cusp of his grip, where his other hand reaches to support the formidable power conjured. He lies below the beast while still on the ground, and in a jolt of thrusting vigor, lugs the strength into a lodge through a sternum without chance. It shoots up and through the beast. The blow causes blood to cough up through the devil’s mouth before his head rolls to the side, where the spine grows in stretching clicks and pops of a back. It continues to run through the goat—bull, where the beast simply dies limply on the spear, held up by Samson’s grasp… Its weight is too much, and so Samson yanks it left way, throwing the monster into the pond’s water. Splashes fly as the smell of a wet dog exudes, the water mixing into a dark blood wine.",
}
